ion behavior is in scope for that child, since it is only listed under criteria 3 and 5."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the Child decomposition, amend the delivery child to read 'It delivers criteria 3, 5 and 7'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the extra_headers capability assertion for rebar's ACTUAL provider classes: confirm (with a cited upstream reference or an end-to-end wire-capture test) that ModelSettings.extra_headers is read and sent by the concrete OpenAI-compatible model class behind _RebarOpenAICompatibleProvider AND by the custom retrying AnthropicProvider, rather than relying on the generic 'documented for OpenAI, Anthropic, ...' claim (cf. upstream issue #6843 where a listed provider silently drops it).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'It is upstream-supported (pydantic_ai/settings.py, documented for OpenAI, Anthropic, Bedrock, Google and others)'","Retrieved: pydantic-ai GitHub issue #6843 title 'ModelSettings.timeout and ModelSettings.extra_headers document xAI under Supported by:, but models/xai.py never reads either one. Both are silently dropped.' — extra_headers support is per-provider and being listed does not guarantee it is read.","Codebase: rebar delivers through custom shapes — _RebarOpenAICompatibleProvider wrapping a self-built httpx.AsyncClient (src/rebar/llm/providers.py:295-305) and a custom retrying AnthropicProvider built on a self-built AsyncAnthropic client (src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:155-165) — not the vanilla model constructions the upstream docs enumerate.","This is an unverified capability assertion (T1 check c): 'library supports X' is asserted for a generic model set, but the load-bearing question is whether extra_headers is honored by the two specific model classes rebar instantiates."],"finding":"The plan asserts pydantic-ai's ModelSettings.extra_headers is 'documented for OpenAI, Anthropic, Bedrock, Google and others' but does not verify the header actually reaches the wire through rebar's OWN custom provider constructions; upstream evidence shows extra_headers is a per-provider concern where a listed provider can silently drop it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc553434d43fd96f3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, second Rationale bullet ('ModelSettings.extra_headers beats patching httpx clients')","norm_id":"n78af8ddfba7c0108","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator configures a per-run correlation header; delivery silently drops it because the concrete pydantic-ai model class backing rebar's OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic provider does not forward extra_headers on the code path in use, and the gateway keeps seeing anonymous calls.","criteria 3/4/5 pass in tests using TestModel/a stub yet fail against the real provider whose model class ignores extra_headers."],"severity":